# Water-operations SITL MODE layer. Apply drone -> this file -> mission.parm.
# Simulation-only: NEVER upload this layer to a real aircraft. It overrides the
# physical drone profile for idealized rangefinder behavior. Shared precision
# landing settings now live in mission.parm, not this file. --no-rc provides an
# earlier baseline; later explicit user overlays can override that baseline.
# Native type-100 data goes through ArduPilot's real rangefinder frontend, not
# invented MOOS navigation/readiness. No EKF source/arming/flight-mode changes.
# Real protocol, noise, latency, glare, water response and dead zones are NOT
# replicated; successful SITL results cannot certify the installed sensor.
# Type-100 source:
# https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/dbe792162d06cab66c3475fd5556bf7a120f119e/libraries/AP_RangeFinder/AP_RangeFinder_SITL.cpp
# Metadata: https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/dbe792162d06cab66c3475fd5556bf7a120f119e/libraries/AP_RangeFinder/AP_RangeFinder_Params.cpp

# RNGFND1_TYPE -- enum: 0 disabled, 1 analog, 100 native SITL (selected).
# Read the simulator's range through ArduPilot's native backend. No additional
# app, analog pin/scaling or serial endpoint is needed. Do not copy to hardware.
# This is independent of PLND_TYPE=1 (external MAVLink target) in mission.parm.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#rngfnd1-type
RNGFND1_TYPE 100

# SIM_SONAR_ROT -- simulated beam orientation enum, 25 = PITCH_270 (down).
# Match the drone's downward RNGFND1_ORIENT=25. Simulator attitude and mounting
# geometry determine measured slant range to the surface; this is not UAV yaw,
# a precision-target mounting correction, or deck-edge detection.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#sim-sonar-rot
SIM_SONAR_ROT 25

# RNGFND1_MIN -- reliable minimum range, metres. User-approved SITL override 0
# replaces the physical 0.15 m minimum, so zero/near-ground simulated readings
# can become Good after native validation samples. This deliberately removes
# the hardware dead zone; it is not a physical mounting/surface correction.
# PLND_ALT_MIN=0 separately disables a blind-finish height exception. Native
# health, freshness and geometry checks still apply; nothing fabricates flight
# readiness. MAX=12 m remains inherited from the selected physical drone file.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#rngfnd1-min
RNGFND1_MIN 0

# RNGFND1_GNDCLR -- expected grounded range, metres. User-approved SITL value 0
# replaces physical 0.17 m, matching the zero-height idealized fixture rather
# than real landing-gear/sensor mounting. It does not move the beam or tell LAND
# to stop at zero. Although metadata lists 0.05..1.5 m, zero is a deliberate
# simulation-only override; EKF3 still floors its on-ground assumption at 0.05 m.
# Real sensor clearance remains in the drone profile. No frontend/estimator
# readiness is manufactured, and the zero override MUST NOT reach REAL.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#rngfnd1-gndclr
# EKF floor: libraries/AP_NavEKF3/AP_NavEKF3_Measurements.cpp::readRangeFinder
RNGFND1_GNDCLR 0

# Precision-target virtual sensor mounting: upstream PLND_CAM_POS_X/Y/Z are
# body-frame offsets in metres, each documented -5..5 m (0.01 m increments).
# pMavlinkLandingTarget's synthetic observation uses the native vehicle position
# as its virtual sensor origin; no separate camera translation is modeled.
# User-approved zero offsets belong ONLY in this SITL mode layer, not the
# shared mission: REAL mounting is unmeasured and must remain inherited.
# These offsets are not Home/deck heights, rangefinder GNDCLR/beam mounting,
# UAV yaw alignment, desired landing offsets or permission to land. They do
# not move the physical simulator/ship, repair timing, manufacture health or
# imply a real camera is at the vehicle origin. Origin/axis conventions must
# agree with the observation producer to avoid missing/double compensation.
# No custom patch is introduced by these upstream precision-sensor parameters.
# Source: libraries/AC_PrecLand/AC_PrecLand.cpp, var_info/construct_pos_meas/
# run_output_prediction, reviewed companion ArduPilot 4.7.1.

# PLND_CAM_POS_X -- forward offset, metres; upstream: "Positive X is forward
# of the origin." Set 0 because the virtual camera has no forward translation.
# A nonzero guess would alter native target-position compensation, not physically
# mount a camera. Only the simulation convention is selected by this choice.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#plnd-cam-pos-x
PLND_CAM_POS_X 0

# PLND_CAM_POS_Y -- right offset, metres; upstream: "Positive Y is to the right
# of the origin." Set 0 for the same vehicle-origin virtual sensor, with no
# lateral translation. This is not PEARL's relative bearing or lateral landing
# clearance; zero neither centers the aircraft nor proves target acquisition.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#plnd-cam-pos-y
PLND_CAM_POS_Y 0

# PLND_CAM_POS_Z -- down offset, metres; upstream: "Positive Z is down from
# the origin." Set 0 because no vertical virtual-camera translation is modeled.
# This does not change deck MSL, rangefinder mounting/clearance, target slant
# range or touchdown detection. REAL camera height must be measured separately.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#plnd-cam-pos-z
PLND_CAM_POS_Z 0

# Desired landing offsets are upstream PLND_LAND_OFS_X/Y, in CENTIMETRES,
# unlike metre-valued PLND_CAM_POS_*. Each is documented -20..20 cm, 1 cm steps.
# These select camera-to-target landing displacement, not camera mounting.
# User-approved SITL-only zeros request the virtual camera directly over the
# simulated target, without a deliberate forward/right landing displacement.
# Native output prediction rotates any nonzero body-frame offset into NED
# using aircraft attitude, not PEARL's yaw, and adds it to the landing estimate.
# That estimate is also used for the horizontal descent gate and remembered
# target retry location. Zero adds no such displacement; it does not repair
# geometry/timing errors, force accurate touchdown, create deck containment or
# bypass native target/height validity, FSM clearance or landing authority.
# This is upstream behavior, not a simulator geometry or recovery-policy patch.
# Source: libraries/AC_PrecLand/AC_PrecLand.cpp, var_info/run_output_prediction,
# reviewed companion Copter 4.7.1. REAL offsets remain unselected/commented.

# PLND_LAND_OFS_X -- desired forward landing displacement, cm; upstream:
# "Desired landing position of the camera forward of the target in vehicle
# body frame." Set 0 for a centered virtual-camera objective. Positive selects
# forward, negative aft; this is not a Home/deck coordinate or a mount offset.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#plnd-land-ofs-x
PLND_LAND_OFS_X 0

# PLND_LAND_OFS_Y -- desired right landing displacement, cm; upstream:
# "desired landing position of the camera right of the target in vehicle
# body frame." Set 0 for the same centered objective. Positive selects right,
# negative left; zero adds no lateral objective but does not guarantee physical
# touchdown alignment or prove the real aircraft should use this same value.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#plnd-land-ofs-y
PLND_LAND_OFS_Y 0

# SIM_PLD_ENABLE -- enable the native SITL precision-landing device (boolean).
# Official parameter metadata: "Allows you to enable (1) or disable (0) the
# Preland simulation". Keep 0: this mission's synthetic camera is the separate
# MOOS pMavlinkLandingTarget process, using the MAVLink backend above.
# This disables the built-in simulated beacon/device, NOT precision landing
# itself and NOT the external MAVLink stream. Range/stale-geometry failures
# should be visible through that stream rather than hidden by a native target.
# Native simulated-beacon position, radiance and range parameters are therefore
# not part of this mission's target geometry configuration.
# Official metadata / implementation:
# https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/SITL/SIM_Precland.cpp
# Parameter: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#sim-pld-enable
SIM_PLD_ENABLE    0

# SIM_SHIP_ENABLE -- enable SITL's ship/deck model (boolean).
# Official parameter metadata: "Enable ship landing simulation"; 0 disables,
# 1 enables. Use 1 so the patched simulator can provide an elevated physical
# surface and carry the grounded UAV with PEARL; target observations alone
# cannot create that surface or simulate elevated contact.
# With SIM_SHIP_EXT=1 below, the patch requires a valid fresh external pose:
# enabling this parameter alone does not activate a deck at startup.
# The UAV-owned pMavlinkShipBridge streams while SIM_UAV_ON_SHIP=true:
# initially disarmed/on deck, disabled on takeoff exit, reenabled on cleared
# approach, and retained after touchdown. Deck and target share --deck_altitude,
# in MSL metres, while the mission's SITL home is 0 m MSL.
# Official metadata / implementation:
# https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/SITL/SIM_Ship.cpp
# Parameter: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#sim-ship-enable
# Modified behavior: companion ardupilot-sitl/patches/external-ship.patch.
SIM_SHIP_ENABLE   1

# SIM_SHIP_EXT -- CUSTOM PATCH parameter, not an upstream ArduPilot option.
# Patch description: "Use GLOBAL_POSITION_INT from SIM_SHIP_SYSID instead of
# the internal circular trajectory". Value 1 selects external MAVLink deck
# position, MSL altitude, velocity and heading; 0 uses the native trajectory.
# pMavlinkShipBridge supplies these poses from PEARL, independently of the
# precision-target broadcaster. No valid pose, or a pose older than 1000 ms
# of ArduPilot simulated time, makes the external deck surface unavailable.
# SAFETY/LIMITATION: the patch has NO horizontal proximity gate. While active,
# its MSL height replaces the ground surface even off-deck, and grounded UAVs
# are attached to the supplied ship center. Do not enable pose streaming for
# an off-deck contingency landing. Initial pre-takeoff streaming is intentional
# here: this mission begins grounded on PEARL, not detached on shore. Disable
# it for any off-deck start; do not treat enablement as actual attachment proof.
# Fresh poses must continue
# after recovery to retain the raised deck and carry the recovered aircraft.
# No official documentation exists for this extension. Authoritative source:
# companion ardupilot-sitl/patches/external-ship.patch (ShipSim::var_info,
# get_external_location/get_location, and Aircraft::update_dynamics).
# Relative source: ../../../../ardupilot-sitl/patches/external-ship.patch
SIM_SHIP_EXT      1

# SIM_SHIP_SYSID -- ship's MAVLink system ID (integer; use a distinct vehicle ID).
# Official parameter metadata: "System ID of the ship"; upstream default is 17.
# The custom external-pose patch also uses this ID to filter incoming
# GLOBAL_POSITION_INT senders. Set 17 to match pMavlinkShipBridge's
# ship_system_id=17 in meta_uav.moos. UAV target observations use system 1
# and must not be mistaken for deck poses. A mismatch silently prevents valid
# external deck acquisition, even if the TCP simulation link is connected.
# This is sender selection, NOT authentication or a MOOS community name.
# Official metadata / implementation:
# https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/SITL/SIM_Ship.cpp
# Parameter: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#sim-ship-sysid
# Additional receive-filter behavior: ardupilot-sitl/patches/external-ship.patch,
# ShipSim::handle_external_position.
SIM_SHIP_SYSID    17

# SIM_SHIP_SPEED -- speed of the native ship trajectory, in metres/second.
# Official parameter metadata: "Speed of the ship"; native default is 3 m/s.
# Set 0 so an internal trajectory, if deliberately selected, does not drive
# an independently moving synthetic boat. This is NOT PEARL's mission speed.
# With SIM_SHIP_EXT=1, the patch bypasses the native trajectory and derives
# ship speed/ground motion from external pose velocity instead; PEARL can
# still move at --speed and drift during its hold despite this value 0.
# This value neither freezes MOOS PEARL nor cancels external deck motion.
# Official metadata / implementation:
# https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/SITL/SIM_Ship.cpp
# Parameter: https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#sim-ship-speed
# External-mode override: ardupilot-sitl/patches/external-ship.patch,
# ShipSim::update and ShipSim::apply_external_position.
SIM_SHIP_SPEED    0
